{
  "id": "al13",
  "title": "Subroutines",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "al13-l1",
      "title": "CALL and RET",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "CALL (315) jumps to a subroutine, but first remembers where it came from. RET (311) at the end of the subroutine goes back to right after the CALL.",
        "So the same piece of code can be used from many places: write it once, CALL it often.",
        "Subroutines go after the main program's HLT, so they're only ever reached through CALL."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "076   ; 000: MVI A",
          "003   ;      3",
          "315   ; 002: CALL triple",
          "017   ;      address 017 (low byte)",
          "000   ;      (high byte)",
          "323   ; 005: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "076   ; 007: MVI A",
          "012   ;      10",
          "315   ; 011: CALL triple",
          "017   ;      address 017 (low byte)",
          "000   ;      (high byte)",
          "323   ; 014: OUT 377",
          "377   ;      port 377",
          "166   ; 016: HLT",
          "107   ; 017: MOV B,A   ← triple",
          "207   ; 020: ADD A",
          "200   ; 021: ADD B",
          "311   ; 022: RET"
        ],
        "output": [
          "LEDS ○○○○●○○● = 9",
          "LEDS ○○○●●●●○ = 30"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "al13-l1-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does CALL do that JMP doesn't?",
          "options": [
            "It remembers where to come back to",
            "It's faster",
            "It shows A",
            "Nothing"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "RET uses that remembered address."
        },
        {
          "id": "al13-l1-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does RET do?",
          "options": [
            "Goes back to right after the CALL",
            "Stops the program",
            "Returns to address 000",
            "Clears A"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "RETurn."
        },
        {
          "id": "al13-l1-e3",
          "type": "switches",
          "prompt": "Set the switches to CALL (3 1 5).",
          "answer": 205,
          "explanation": "11 001 101."
        },
        {
          "id": "al13-l1-e4",
